{
  "slug": "dots-glass",
  "format": "reel",
  "size": [
    1080,
    1920
  ],
  "music": "cc0/fresh-focus",
  "padSeconds": 0.25,
  "names": [
    "ChatGPT",
    "Slack",
    "OpenAI"
  ],
  "keywords": [
    "dot",
    "always-on",
    "computer",
    "freedom",
    "password",
    "catch",
    "reset",
    "mistakes",
    "trust"
  ],
  "voice": {
    "engine": "gemini",
    "model": "gemini-2.5-flash-preview-tts",
    "name": "Charon",
    "style": "You are a calm, thoughtful narrator for a premium, late-night tech film: low, smooth and intimate, a hint of wonder at 3 a.m., measured and assured, letting the important lines land softly; serious and honest on the catch. Never dramatic, never announcer-like. Pace: unhurried, about two and a quarter words per second, with a real pause after each question and between thoughts; never rush. Read every word exactly as written.",
    "minPause": {
      "sentence": 0.65,
      "comma": 0.28
    }
  },
  "scenes": [
    {
      "id": "s01",
      "type": "stage",
      "say": "It's 3 a.m. A bug report lands in Slack. By the time you wake up, a fix is waiting for you to review.",
      "beats": [
        {
          "target": "bug",
          "word": "bug",
          "sfx": "pop"
        },
        {
          "target": "slack",
          "word": "Slack",
          "sfx": "pop"
        },
        {
          "target": "fix",
          "word": "fix",
          "sfx": "ding"
        },
        {
          "target": "review",
          "word": "review",
          "sfx": "pop"
        }
      ],
      "section": "dark"
    },
    {
      "id": "s02",
      "type": "stage",
      "say": "That's a dot. It's an always-on agent inside ChatGPT, and it keeps working even after you close the chat.",
      "beats": [
        {
          "target": "dot",
          "word": "dot",
          "sfx": "pop"
        },
        {
          "target": "always",
          "word": "always-on",
          "sfx": "pop"
        },
        {
          "target": "close",
          "word": "close",
          "sfx": "whoosh"
        }
      ],
      "section": "blue"
    },
    {
      "id": "s03",
      "type": "stage",
      "say": "So how does it do that? It gets its very own cloud computer, with its own browser. So it doesn't just talk. It actually does the work.",
      "beats": [
        {
          "target": "computer",
          "word": "computer",
          "sfx": "pop"
        },
        {
          "target": "browser",
          "word": "browser",
          "sfx": "pop"
        },
        {
          "target": "talk",
          "word": "talk",
          "sfx": "tick"
        },
        {
          "target": "work",
          "word": "work",
          "sfx": "ding"
        }
      ],
      "section": "light"
    },
    {
      "id": "s04",
      "type": "stage",
      "say": "You give it a goal, connect the apps it needs, and it brings the results back for you to review.",
      "beats": [
        {
          "target": "goal",
          "word": "goal",
          "sfx": "pop"
        },
        {
          "target": "apps",
          "word": "apps",
          "sfx": "pop"
        },
        {
          "target": "results",
          "word": "results",
          "sfx": "ding"
        }
      ],
      "section": "light"
    },
    {
      "id": "s05",
      "type": "stage",
      "say": "And it doesn't always wait to be asked. It can run scheduled checks, like going through your calendar every morning.",
      "beats": [
        {
          "target": "wait",
          "word": "wait"
        },
        {
          "target": "scheduled",
          "word": "scheduled",
          "sfx": "pop"
        },
        {
          "target": "calendar",
          "word": "calendar",
          "sfx": "tick"
        }
      ],
      "section": "light"
    },
    {
      "id": "s06",
      "type": "stage",
      "say": "Now, the part I really like: you decide how much freedom it gets. It can act on its own, act only when you asked, ask you first, or hand the task back to you.",
      "beats": [
        {
          "target": "freedom",
          "word": "freedom",
          "sfx": "pop"
        },
        {
          "target": "l1",
          "word": "own",
          "sfx": "tick"
        },
        {
          "target": "l2",
          "word": "asked",
          "sfx": "tick"
        },
        {
          "target": "l3",
          "word": "first",
          "sfx": "tick"
        },
        {
          "target": "l4",
          "word": "hand",
          "sfx": "tick"
        }
      ],
      "section": "yellow"
    },
    {
      "id": "s07",
      "type": "stage",
      "say": "And some things, like changing a password, it will always leave to you.",
      "beats": [
        {
          "target": "password",
          "word": "password",
          "sfx": "pop"
        },
        {
          "target": "you",
          "word": "leave",
          "sfx": "stamp"
        }
      ],
      "section": "yellow"
    },
    {
      "id": "s08",
      "type": "stage",
      "say": "Here's the catch. Disconnect an app, and what your dot already learned from it stays.",
      "beats": [
        {
          "target": "catch",
          "word": "catch"
        },
        {
          "target": "disconnect",
          "word": "Disconnect",
          "sfx": "whoosh"
        },
        {
          "target": "stays",
          "word": "stays",
          "sfx": "ding"
        }
      ],
      "section": "dark"
    },
    {
      "id": "s09",
      "type": "stage",
      "say": "The only way to wipe that is a reset, which deletes the whole dot.",
      "beats": [
        {
          "target": "wipe",
          "word": "wipe"
        },
        {
          "target": "reset",
          "word": "reset",
          "sfx": "pop"
        },
        {
          "target": "deletes",
          "word": "deletes",
          "sfx": "whoosh"
        }
      ],
      "section": "dark"
    },
    {
      "id": "s10",
      "type": "stage",
      "say": "And yes, it can still make mistakes, even while following your rules. So check its work.",
      "beats": [
        {
          "target": "mistakes",
          "word": "mistakes",
          "sfx": "stamp"
        },
        {
          "target": "rules",
          "word": "rules"
        },
        {
          "target": "check",
          "word": "check",
          "sfx": "ding"
        }
      ],
      "section": "dark"
    },
    {
      "id": "s11",
      "type": "stage",
      "say": "My take? Great for ongoing jobs you can review. Start with ask first, and give it more freedom as it earns your trust.",
      "beats": [
        {
          "target": "take",
          "word": "take"
        },
        {
          "target": "ongoing",
          "word": "ongoing"
        },
        {
          "target": "start",
          "word": "Start",
          "sfx": "pop"
        },
        {
          "target": "trust",
          "word": "trust",
          "sfx": "ding"
        }
      ],
      "section": "blue"
    },
    {
      "id": "s12",
      "type": "stage",
      "say": "What should I explain next? Tell me in the comments.",
      "beats": [
        {
          "target": "q",
          "word": "What"
        },
        {
          "target": "tell",
          "word": "Tell",
          "sfx": "pop"
        }
      ],
      "section": "dark"
    }
  ],
  "stage": {
    "kit": "hyperframes-glass",
    "html": "stage/stage.html",
    "css": "stage/stage.css",
    "js": "stage/stage.js"
  },
